hadiths[139]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23042","Hushaym narrated to us: Mansur informed us, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Hittan ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take from me, take from me; Allah has made for them a way: virgin with virgin, one hundred lashes and exile for a year; previously married with previously married, one hundred lashes and stoning."
"23043","Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek it in the ninth, the seventh, and the fifth, meaning Laylat al-Qadr."
"23044","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Khalid al-Hadhdha informed us, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, Khalid said: I think he mentioned it on the authority of Abu Asma: Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a pledge from us as he took from women, six: that you not associate anything with Allah, not steal, not commit adultery, not kill your children, that none of you backbite another, and not disobey me in good; so whoever of you commits a prescribed punishment from among them and his punishment is hastened, it is his expiation, and if it is delayed for him, his affair is to Allah, exalted: if He wills He punishes him, and if He wills He has mercy on him."
"23045","Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: I heard Abu Qilabah narrating, on the authority of Abu al-Ashath, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"23046","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: I heard Abu Qilabah narrating, on the authority of Abu al-Ashath, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a pledge from us as he took from women, or from people, and he mentioned its meaning."
"23047","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us and recited, and the recitation became heavy upon him. When he finished he said: Do you recite? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: You must not do so except with the Fatihah of the Book, for there is no prayer except with it."
"23048","Muhammad ibn Abi Adiy narrated to us, on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us wanting to inform us of Laylat al-Qadr, then two men quarreled. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I came out wanting to inform you of Laylat al-Qadr, then two men quarreled, so it was lifted, and perhaps it is better for you; so seek it in the ninth, the seventh, or the fifth."
"23049","al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: al-Awzai narrated to us: Umayr ibn Hani al-Ansi narrated to me: Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah narrated to me, he said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to me, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever wakes at night and says: There is no god but Allah alone, no partner for Him; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable; glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, Allah is greatest, and there is no power nor strength except in Allah; then says: My Lord, forgive me, or he said: Then supplicates to Him, he will be answered; then if he resolves, performs wudu, then prays, his prayer will be accepted."
"23050","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Thabit al-Bunani and Humayd informed us, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he came out one night to his companions wanting to inform them of Laylat al-Qadr, and he mentioned the hadith, except that he said: So seek it in the last ten, in the ninth, the seventh, or the fifth."
"23051","al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: al-Awzai narrated to us: Umayr ibn Hani narrated to me that Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah narrated to him, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah alone, no partner for Him, and that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger, and that Isa is the servant of Allah and His messenger, His word cast to Maryam and a spirit from Him, and that Paradise is true and the Fire is true, Allah, blessed and exalted, will admit him to Paradise according to what he did."
"23052","al-Walid narrated to us: Ibn Jabir narrated to me that he heard Umayr ibn Hani narrating this hadith, on the authority of Junadah, on the authority of Ubadah, on the authority of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it, except that he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, will admit him to Paradise through its eight gates; whichever he wishes he enters."
"23053","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, as a narration reaching the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There is no prayer for one who does not recite with the Fatihah of the Book."
"23054","Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Idris al-Khawlani, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a gathering, and he said: Pledge to me that you not associate anything with Allah, not steal, not commit adultery, and not kill your children. He recited the verse taken over women: When the believing women come to you. So whoever of you fulfills, his reward is upon Allah; and whoever commits something of that and is punished for it, it is expiation for him; and whoever commits something of that and Allah, blessed and exalted, conceals it for him, it is to Allah: if He wills He forgives him, and if He wills He punishes him. Sufyan said: al-Hudhali said to me: Memorize this hadith for me, and it is with al-Zuhri. al-Hudhali said to me: Abu Bakr never narrated the like of this at all, meaning al-Zuhri."
"23055","Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit: He heard it from his grandfather, and Sufyan once said: On the authority of his grandfather Ubadah, Sufyan said: And Ubadah is a naqib, and he is among the seven. We pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hearing and obedience in hardship and ease, activity and dislike, and that we not dispute the command with its people, we speak the truth wherever we are, not fearing in Allah the blame of a blamer. Sufyan said: Some people added: Unless you see open disbelief."
"23056","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abu Sallam al-Araj, on the authority of al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Strive in the path of Allah, for jihad in the path of Allah, blessed and exalted, is a gate among the gates of Paradise by which Allah, blessed and exalted, saves from worry and grief."
"23057","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yisaf, on the authority of Abu al-Muthanna, on the authority of the son of the wife of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): There will be leaders whom things distract, delaying prayer from its time; so pray prayer at its time, and make your prayer with them voluntary."
"23058","Hajjaj narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, on the authority of Abu al-Muthanna, on the authority of the son of the wife of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the like of it."
"23059","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qilabah, on the authority of Abu al-Ashath, he said: People were selling silver from the spoils for stipends. Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gold for gold, silver for silver, dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, and salt for salt, except equal for equal, like for like; so whoever increases and seeks increase has committed riba."
"23060","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, on the authority of Shubah, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Hafs narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn al-Musabbih, or Abu al-Musabbih, on the authority of Ibn al-Simt, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Abdullah ibn Rawahah, and did not move aside from his bed for him. He said: Who are the martyrs of my ummah? They said: The killing of a Muslim is martyrdom. He said: Then the martyrs of my ummah are few: the killing of a Muslim is martyrdom, plague is martyrdom, belly disease and drowning, and the woman killed by her child while she is jam, all together."
"23061","He said: Waki narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn al-Ghaz narrated to us, on the authority of Ubadah ibn Nusayy, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you count the martyr among you? They said: The one who fights and is killed in the path of Allah, exalted. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the martyrs of my ummah are few: the killed in the path of Allah, blessed and exalted, is a martyr; the plague-struck is a martyr; the belly-diseased is a martyr; and the woman who dies in jum, a martyr, meaning the postpartum woman."
"23062","Waki narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, on the authority of Abu al-Muthanna al-Himsi, on the authority of Abu Ubayy, son of the wife of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be over you leaders whom things distract from prayer until they delay it from its time; so pray it at its time. He said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, if I catch it with them, shall I pray? He said: If you wish."
"23063","Waki narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about His saying, blessed and exalted: For them is glad tidings in worldly life and in the Hereafter. He said: It is the righteous dream the Muslim sees or that is seen for him."
"23064","Affan narrated to us: Aban narrated to us: Yahya narrated to me, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saying: O Messenger of Allah, what about the saying of Allah, blessed and exalted: For them is glad tidings in worldly life and in the Hereafter? He said: You have asked me about something no one of my ummah asked me about, or no one before you. He said: It is the righteous dream the righteous man sees or that is seen for him."
"23065","Waki narrated to us: Mughirah ibn Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Ubadah ibn Nusayy, on the authority of al-Aswad ibn Thalabah, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: I taught people of the Suffah writing and the Quran, and a man among them gifted me a bow, it is not wealth to me, and I shoot with it in the path of Allah, blessed and exalted. I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: If it pleases you to be collared with a collar of fire, then accept it."
"23066","Yamar, meaning Ibn Bishr, narrated to us: Abdullah informed us: Sufyan informed us, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Hilal ibn Yasaf, on the authority of Abu al-Muthanna al-Himsi, on the authority of Abu Ubayy, son of the wife of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O people, leaders will come whom things distract until they do not pray prayer at its appointed time; so pray prayer at its appointed time. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, then shall we pray with them? He said: Yes. Abdullah said: My father said, may Allah have mercy on him: And this is correct."
"23067","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, and he mentioned it, he said: On the authority of the son of the wife of Ubadah, on the authority of Ubadah, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the like of it."
"23068","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hammad, that is Hammad ibn Salamah, informed us, on the authority of Jabalah ibn Atiyyah, on the authority of Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of his grandfather Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fights in the path of Allah intending in his fighting only a hobble, then for him is what he intended."
"23069","Yazid narrated to us: Yahya, meaning Ibn Said, informed us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, that Ibn Muhayriz al-Qurashi, then al-Jumahi, informed him, and he was in Sham and had met Muawiyah, and informed him that al-Mukhdaji, a man from Banu Kinanah, informed him that a man from the Ansar in Sham known as Abu Muhammad informed him that witr is obligatory. al-Mukhdaji mentioned that he went to Ubadah ibn al-Samit and mentioned to him that Abu Muhammad says witr is obligatory. Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: Abu Muhammad lied; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Five prayers Allah, blessed and exalted, prescribed upon servants; whoever brings them without neglecting any of them, belittling their right, he has a covenant with Allah, blessed and exalted, to admit him to Paradise; and whoever does not bring them, he has no covenant with Allah: if He wills He punishes him, and if He wills He forgives him."
"23070","Yazid narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Mahmud ibn al-Rabi, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with us the dawn prayer, and the recitation became heavy upon him. When he finished he said: I see you recite behind your imam. They said: Yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, we do this. He said: Then do not do so except with the Mother of the Quran, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite with it."
"23071","Yazid said: Hammam ibn Yahya narrated to us: Affan narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, on the authority of Ata ibn Yasar, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Paradise is one hundred degrees; between every two degrees is a march of one hundred years, and Affan said: Like between heaven to earth; and al-Firdaws is its highest degree, from it the four rivers emerge, and the Throne is above it; and when you ask Allah, blessed and exalted, ask Him for al-Firdaws."
"23072","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him; and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him."
"23073","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatadah, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik narrating, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: The dream of the Muslim is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"23074","Rawh narrated to us: Said narrated to us, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the Muslim is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"23075","Abu al-Yaman and Ishaq ibn Isa both said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Maryam, on the authority of Abu Sallam, Ishaq said: al-Araj, on the authority of al-Miqdam ibn Madi Karib al-Kindi, that he sat with Ubadah ibn al-Samit, Abu al-Darda, and al-Harith ibn Muawiyah al-Kindi, and they recalled the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abu al-Darda said to Ubadah: O Ubadah, the words of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in such-and-such campaign concerning the fifths. Ubadah said, Ishaq said in his hadith: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them in their campaign beside a camel from the division; when he finished the salutation, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, took a hair between his fingers, and said: This is among your spoils, and there is nothing for me in it except my share with you, except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you; so return the thread and the needle, and greater than that and smaller, and do not steal from spoils, for ghulul is fire and shame upon its people in this world and the Hereafter. Strive against people for Allah, blessed and exalted, near and far, and do not care in Allah the blame of a blamer. Establish the limits of Allah in residence and travel, and strive in the path of Allah, for jihad is a great gate among the gates of Paradise by which Allah, blessed and exalted, saves from distress and worry."
"23076","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ishaq: Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to me, on the authority of his father al-Walid, on the authority of his grandfather Ubadah ibn al-Samit, and he was one of the naqibs, he said: We pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the pledge of war, and Ubadah was among the twelve who pledged in the first Aqabah upon the pledge of women, in hearing and obedience in our hardship and ease, our activity and dislike, and that we not dispute the command with its people, and that we speak the truth wherever we are, not fearing in Allah the blame of a blamer."
"23077","Surayj ibn al-Numan narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of al-Mughirah, on the authority of al-Shabi, that Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There is no man wounded in his body with a wound and then gives it in charity except Allah expiates from him the like of what he gave in charity."
"23078","Surayj narrated to us: al-Muafa narrated to us: Mughirah ibn Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Ubadah ibn Nusayy, on the authority of al-Aswad ibn Thalabah, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I was sick, among people of the Ansar visiting me, and said: Do you know what the martyr is? They were silent. He said: Do you know what the martyr is? They were silent. He said: Do you know what the martyr is? I said to my wife: Prop me up, so she propped me. I said: Whoever embraces Islam, then emigrates, then is killed in the path of Allah, is a martyr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the martyrs of my ummah are few: killing in the path of Allah is martyrdom, belly disease is martyrdom, drowning is martyrdom, and the postpartum woman is martyrdom."
"23079","Affan narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us: Qatadah and Humayd informed us, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Hittan ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when revelation descended upon him, was distressed by it and his face changed color; and when he was relieved from it he said: Take from me, take from me, three times; Allah has made for them a way: previously married with previously married, and virgin with virgin: previously married, one hundred lashes and stoning; and virgin, one hundred lashes and exile for a year."
"23080","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata ibn Yasar, on the authority of Abdullah al-Sunabihi, he said: Abu Muhammad claimed that witr is obligatory. Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: Abu Muhammad lied; I bear witness I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Five prayers Allah obligated upon His servants; whoever perfects their wudu and their prayer at their times, completing their bowing, their prostration, and their humility, he has a covenant with Allah to forgive him; and whoever does not do so, he has no covenant with Allah: if He wills He forgives him, and if He wills He punishes him."
"23081","Abu al-Ala al-Hasan ibn Sawwar narrated to us: Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Ziyad: Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah narrated to me: My father narrated to me, he said: I entered upon Ubadah while he was sick, imagining death in him. I said: O my father, advise me and strive for me. He said: Seat me. He said: O my son, you will not taste the taste of faith, nor reach the true reality of knowledge of Allah, blessed and exalted, until you believe in qadar, its good and its evil. He said: I said: O my father, how can I know what is the good of qadar and its evil? He said: You know that what missed you was never to befall you, and what befell you was never to miss you. O my son, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first thing Allah, blessed and exalted, created is the Pen; then He said: Write. So it flowed in that hour with what will be until the Day of Resurrection. O my son, if you die and you are not upon that, you will enter the Fire."
"23082","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, on the authority of al-Harith ibn Yazid, on the authority of Ali ibn Rabah, that a man heard Ubadah ibn al-Samit saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us, and Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Stand, we seek help through the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) against this hypocrite. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One does not stand for me; one stands only for Allah, blessed and exalted."
"23083","Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: My father advised me, may Allah have mercy on him, saying: O my son, I advise you to believe in qadar, its good and its evil, for if you do not believe, Allah, blessed and exalted, will admit you to the Fire. He said: And I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The first thing Allah, blessed and exalted, created is the Pen; then He said to it: Write. He said: And what shall I write? He said: So write what will be and what is to be until the Hour rises."
"23084","Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Jafar narrated to us: Anas ibn Iyad Abu Damrah narrated to me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah narrated to me, on the authority of Yala ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz, that Abdullah ibn Abbad al-Zuraqi informed him that he used to hunt sparrows in the well of Ihab, and it belonged to them, he said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit saw me having taken a sparrow, and he takes it from me and releases it, saying: O my son, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared sacred what is between its two lava tracts, as Ibrahim declared Makkah sacred."
"23085","Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us: Sad ibn Aws al-Katib narrated to us, on the authority of Bilal ibn Yahya al-Ansi, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, on the authority of Thabit ibn al-Simt, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A group of my ummah will deem wine lawful under a name they call it by."
"23086","Muhammad ibn Bakr, Rawh, and Abd al-Razzaq said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: And Sulayman ibn Musa also said: Kathir ibn Murrah narrated to us that Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no soul on earth that dies having good with Allah, blessed and exalted, that loves to return to you except the killed one, and Rawh said: Except the killed in the path of Allah, for he loves to return and be killed another time."
"23087","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, on the authority of al-Sunabihi, that he said: I entered upon Ubadah ibn al-Samit while he was dying, and I wept. He said: Wait, why do you weep? By Allah, if I am martyred I will testify for you, and if intercession is granted to me I will intercede for you, and if I am able I will benefit you. Then he said: By Allah, no hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which there is good for you except I narrated it to you, except one hadith I will narrate to you today while my soul is encompassed: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever testifies that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, he is forbidden to the Fire."
"23088","Qutaybah, the like of it, he said: Allah, blessed and exalted, forbade the Fire upon him."
"23089","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Salamah, meaning Ibn Abi al-Husam, narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Laylat al-Qadr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Ramadan, seek it in the last ten, for it is in the odd: in twenty-one, twenty-three, twenty-five, twenty-seven, twenty-nine, or in the last night. Whoever stands it seeking it with faith and reckoning, then is granted it, forgiven for him what preceded of his sin and what comes later."
"23090","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Salamah, meaning Ibn Abi al-Husam, narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Laylat al-Qadr. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Ramadan, seek it in the last ten, for it is in the odd: in twenty-one, twenty-three, twenty-five, twenty-seven, twenty-nine, or in the last night. Whoever stands it seeking it with faith and reckoning, then is granted it, forgiven for him what preceded of his sin and what comes later."
"23091","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Ishaq, meaning al-Fazari, narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Musa, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abu Sallam, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Return the thread and the needle, and beware ghulul, for it is shame upon its people on the Day of Resurrection."
"23092","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Said narrated to us, on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of al-Hasan, on the authority of Hittan ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi, on the authority of Ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when revelation descended upon him, distress affected him because of that and his face changed color, upon him be prayer and peace; then Allah, blessed and exalted, sent down one day, and when he was relieved from it he said: Take from me; Allah has made for them a way: previously married with previously married, and virgin with virgin: previously married, one hundred lashes and stoning with stones; and virgin, one hundred lashes then exile for a year."
"23093","Hashim ibn al-Qasim and Affan both said: Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, on the authority of al-Amash, on the authority of al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit, on the authority of his father, he said: We pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hearing and obedience in dislike and activity, hardship and ease, preference over us, and that we establish our tongues with justice wherever we are, not fearing in Allah the blame of a blamer. Affan said: Our tongues."
"23094","Hasan narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: al-Harith ibn Yazid narrated to us, on the authority of Ali ibn Rabah, that he heard Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah saying: I heard Ubadah ibn al-Samit saying: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Prophet of Allah, which deed is best? He said: Faith in Allah, belief in Him, and jihad in His path. He said: I want easier than that, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Tolerance and patience. He said: I want easier than that, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do not accuse Allah, blessed and exalted, in anything He decreed for you."
"23095","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Musa, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abu Sallam, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a hair from the side of a camel and said: O people, nothing of what Allah bestowed upon you is lawful for me to the extent of this except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you."
"23096","Muawiyah narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyash, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Musa, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Abu Umamah, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is jihad in the path of Allah, blessed and exalted, for it is a gate among the gates of Paradise by which Allah removes worry and grief."
"23097","Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, he said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit Abu al-Walid, a Badri, Aqabi, tree-pledge participant, and he is a naqib."
"23098","My father narrated to me: Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya, meaning Ibn Said al-Ansari, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Hibban narrated to me, on the authority of Ibn Muhayriz, on the authority of a man from Banu Kinanah called al-Mukhdaji, he said: There was in Sham a man called Abu Muhammad who said witr is obligatory. He said: So I went to Ubadah and said: Abu Muhammad claims witr is obligatory. He said: Abu Muhammad lied; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Five prayers Allah, exalted, prescribed upon servants; whoever brings them without neglecting any of them, he comes having a covenant with Allah to admit him to Paradise; and whoever neglects them, belittling, he comes having no covenant: if He wills He punishes him, and if He wills He admits him to Paradise."
"23099","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us wanting to inform us of Laylat al-Qadr, then two men quarreled, so it was lifted. He said: I came out wanting to inform you of Laylat al-Qadr, then two men quarreled, so it was lifted; so seek it in the ninth, the seventh, and the fifth."
"23100","Ubaydah narrated to us, and he said: Seek it in the ninth that remains."
"23101","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us from Shu'bah, and Hajjaj said: Shu'bah narrated to me from Qatadah from Anas from Ubadah ibn al-Samit from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said - Hajjaj said in his hadith: I heard Anas from Ubadah ibn al-Samit from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The vision of the believer, or the Muslim, is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"23102","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us from Thabit from Anas from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it."
"23103","Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us from Isma'il, meaning Ibn Abi Khalid: Hakim ibn Jabir narrated to us from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Gold for gold and silver for silver, like for like, until he singled out salt; then Mu'awiyah said: This says nothing to Ubadah; so Ubadah said: I do not care not to be in a land in which Mu'awiyah is; I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say that."
"23104","Waki' narrated to us: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us from Ubadah ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit from his grandfather Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, to hear and obey in hardship and ease, in energy and dislike, not to dispute authority with its people, to speak the truth wherever we are, and not to fear in Allah the blame of any blamer."
"23105","Waki' narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah from Sulayman ibn Musa from Makhul from Abu Sallam al-A'raj from Abu Umamah from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, granted as extra spoils at the outset a fourth and upon return a third."
"23106","Waki' narrated to us from Sufyan from Khalid al-Hadhdha' from Abu Qilabah from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, dates for dates, and salt for salt, like for like, hand to hand; when the kinds differ, sell as you wish when it is hand to hand."
"23107","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi and Bahz both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Jabalah ibn Atiyyah from Ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit from his grandfather Ubadah who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever campaigns in the way of Allah, blessed and exalted, intending in his campaign nothing but a hobble-rope, he shall have what he intended; Bahz said in his hadith: Jabalah ibn Atiyyah narrated to us from Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah."
"23108","Isma'il narrated to us: Salamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us from Ibn Sirin: Muslim ibn Yasar and Abdullah ibn Ubayd, who was called Ibn Hurmuz, narrated to us, saying: The dwelling brought together Ubadah ibn al-Samit and Mu'awiyah, either in a church or in a synagogue; then Ubadah stood and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us gold for gold, silver for silver, dates for dates, wheat for wheat, and barley for barley; and one of them said: and salt for salt, and the other did not say it; and one of them said: Whoever adds or asks for more has engaged in usury, and the other did not say it; and he commanded us to sell gold for silver, silver for gold, wheat for barley, and barley for wheat, hand to hand, as we wish."
"23109","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Hittan ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Take from me; Allah has made for them a way: the previously married with the previously married and the virgin with the virgin; the previously married is flogged and stoned, and the virgin is flogged and exiled."
"23110","Hajjaj narrated to us, saying: I heard Shu'bah narrate from Qatadah, saying: I heard al-Hasan narrate from Hittan ibn Abdullah from Ubadah ibn al-Samit from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of it, meaning the like of the hadith of Ibn Ja'far."
"23111","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us from Khalid, saying: I heard Abu Qilabah narrate from Abu al-Ash'ath from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took upon us what he took upon women - or people -: not to associate anything with Allah, not to steal, not to commit adultery, not to kill our children, not to backbite, that none of us slander another, and not to disobey him in what is right; whoever of you commits a prescribed offense among what was forbidden and it is carried out upon him, it is expiation for him; and whoever is deferred, his affair is to Allah, blessed and exalted: if He wills He punishes him, and if He wills He forgives him."
"23112","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us: Ibn Shihab narrated to me from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, saying: I heard Ubadah ibn al-Samit say: I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, among a group, and he said: I pledge you that you associate nothing with Allah, do not steal, do not commit adultery, do not kill your children, do not bring a slander you fabricate between your hands and your feet, and do not disobey him in what is right; whoever of you fulfills, his reward is upon Allah; and whoever commits any of that then is punished for it, it is purification for him; and whomever Allah conceals, that is to Allah, blessed and exalted: if He wills He punishes him, and if He wills He forgives him."
"23113","Abd al-Razzaq said: Then he is punished for it in this world, it is purification for him - or he said: expiation."
"23114","Abdullah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Sa'id narrated to us from Qatadah from al-Hasan from Hittan ibn Abdullah, brother of Banu Raqash, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when revelation descended upon him, was distressed by it and his face changed color; then one day revelation was sent to him, and when it was lifted from him, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Take from me; Allah has made for them a way: the previously married with the previously married and the virgin with the virgin; the previously married: one hundred lashes then stoning with stones; and the virgin with the virgin: one hundred lashes then exile for a year."
"23115","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to me from Umayr ibn Hani that he narrated to him from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Upon you is hearing and obeying in your hardship and your ease, your energy and your dislike, and preferment against you; and do not dispute authority with its people, even if you see that you have - [source text breaks off here]."
"23116","Al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us from Hayyan Abu al-Nadr that he heard from Junadah narrating from Ubadah the like of it."
"23117","Al-Walid narrated to us, saying: Ibn Thawban narrated to me - perhaps Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban - from Umayr ibn Hani, Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah narrated to him from Ubadah ibn al-Samit from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the like of that; he said: So long as they do not command you to flagrant sin."
"23118","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us: Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us from Ata ibn Yasar from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Paradise is one hundred degrees; between every two degrees of them is as between heaven and earth; al-Firdaws is its highest degree; from it gush the four rivers of Paradise, and above it is the Throne; and when you ask Allah, ask Him for al-Firdaws."
"23119","Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Ibn Mubarak narrated to us from Haywah and Attab, saying: Abdullah narrated to us: Haywah told us from Umar ibn Malik al-Ma'afiri that a man of his people told him that he attended that, the year of al-Madiq: that Ubadah ibn al-Samit told Mu'awiyah, when he asked him about the man who asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for a hobble-rope before distribution, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Leave it until it is distributed - and Attab said: until we distribute - then if you wish we will give you a hobble-rope, and if you wish we will give you many times over."
"23120","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us: Harb narrated to us: Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, narrated to us from Abu Salamah from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that he asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about this verse: For them is glad tidings in the life of this world and in the Hereafter; he said: It is the righteous vision which the servant sees or which is seen for him."
"23121","Abd al-Malik ibn Amr narrated to us: Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Muhammad, meaning Ibn Aqil, from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that he said: O Messenger of Allah, tell us about the Night of Decree; then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is in Ramadan; seek it in the last ten, for it is odd: on the twenty-first, or twenty-third, or twenty-fifth, or twenty-seventh, or twenty-ninth, or on the last night; whoever stands it in faith and seeking reward, forgiven for him what preceded of his sin and what comes after."
"23122","Hashim narrated to us: Layth narrated to us from Yazid ibn Abi Habib from Abu al-Khayr from al-Sunabihi from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that he said: I am of the chiefs who pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; he said: And we pledged him not to associate anything with Allah, not to commit adultery, not to steal, not to kill the soul which Allah forbade, and not to plunder; and if we commit any of that, its judgment is to Allah, blessed and exalted."
"23123","Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: My father narrated to us from Salih, and Ibn Shihab narrated that Mahmud ibn al-Rabi', in whose face the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, spurted water from their well twice, told him that Ubadah ibn al-Samit told him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no prayer for one who does not recite the Opening of the Book."
"23124","Affan narrated to us, and Bahz narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us: Qatadah told us from Anas from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him; and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him."
"23125","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq: Makhul narrated to me from Mahmud ibn Rabi' al-Ansari from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in dawn prayer and the recitation became heavy upon him in it; then when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished his prayer, he turned to us with his face and said: I see you recite behind your imam when he recites aloud; he said: We said: Yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, indeed for this; then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not do so except with the Opening of the Book, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it."
"23126","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq, meaning Muhammad, from Makhul from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi' from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us and recited, and the recitation became heavy upon him; then when he finished he said: Do you recite? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; then: It does you no harm not to do so except with the Opening of the Book, for there is no prayer except with it."
"23127","Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq from Abd al-Rahman from Sulayman ibn Musa from Makhul from Abu Umamah al-Bahili who said: I asked Ubadah ibn al-Samit about the spoils of war; then he said: Concerning us, the company of the men of Badr, it was revealed, when we differed over the extra share and our manners worsened over it; so Allah took it from our hands and gave it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, divided it among the Muslims equally, he says: equally."
"23128","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj told us, saying: Sulayman ibn Musa said: Kathir ibn Murrah narrated to us that Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no soul on earth that dies having good with Allah, mighty and majestic, that would love to return to you though it had the world, except the slain one, for he loves to return and be killed once more."
"23129","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Ma'mar narrated to us from al-Zuhri from Mahmud ibn al-Rabi' from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no prayer for one who does not recite the Opening of the Book and more."
"23130","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to me from Ibn Ishaq: Makhul narrated to me from Mahmud ibn Rabi' al-Ansari from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, led us in dawn prayer and the recitation became heavy upon him; then when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished his prayer, he turned to us with his face and said: I see you recite behind your imam when he recites aloud; he said: We said: Yes, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, this; he said: Then do not do so except with the Opening of the Book, for there is no prayer for one who does not recite it."
"23131","Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan told us from Abd al-Wahid ibn Qays from Ubadah ibn al-Samit from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The substitutes in this community are thirty, like Ibrahim the Friend of the Merciful, mighty and majestic; whenever a man dies, Allah, blessed and exalted, replaces in his place a man; my father, may Allah have mercy on him, said: Concerning it - meaning the hadith of Abd al-Wahhab - there is speech other than this, and it is rejected, meaning the hadith."
"23132","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Habban narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Muhayriz from al-Mukhdaji from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said, from his mouth to my mouth - I do not say so-and-so narrated to me nor so-and-so: Five prayers Allah obligated upon His servants; whoever meets Him with them, not neglecting any of them, meets Him having with Him a covenant by which He admits him to Paradise; and whoever meets Him having diminished any of them, belittling their right, meets Him having no covenant; if He wills He punishes him, and if He wills He forgives him."
"23133","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith and others of his companions narrated to me from Sulayman ibn Musa al-Ashdaq from Makhul from Abu Umamah al-Bahili who said: I asked Ubadah ibn al-Samit about the spoils of war; then he said: Concerning us, the company of the men of Badr, it was revealed, when we differed over the extra share and our manners worsened over it; so Allah, blessed and exalted, took it from our hands and gave it to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, divided it among us equally, he says: equally."
"23134","Ya'qub narrated to us: My father narrated to us from Ibn Ishaq: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to me from Marthad ibn Abdullah al-Yazani from Abu Abdullah Abd al-Rahman ibn Usaylah al-Sunabihi from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I was among those present at the first Aqabah; we were twelve men; then we pledged the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the pledge of women, before fighting was obligated: not to associate anything with Allah, not to steal, not to commit adultery, not to kill our children, not to bring a slander we fabricate between our hands and our feet, and not to disobey him in what is right; if you fulfill, for you is Paradise; and if you commit any of that, your affair is to Allah: if He wills He punishes you, and if He wills He forgives you."
"23135","Harun narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Malik ibn al-Khayr al-Ziyadi narrated to me from Abu Qabil al-Ma'afiri from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: He is not of my community who does not honor our elder, have mercy on our young, and recognize the right of our scholar; Abdullah said: And I heard it myself from Harun."
"23136","Affan narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr ibn Hafs told me, saying: I heard Abu Musabbih - or Ibn Musabbih, Abu Bakr doubted - from Ibn al-Simt from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, visited Abdullah ibn Rawahah; he said: He did not move aside for him from his bed, and he said: Do you know who the martyrs of my community are? They said: A Muslim being killed is martyrdom; he said: Then the martyrs of my community would be few: a Muslim being killed is martyrdom, plague is martyrdom, and a woman whom her child kills in childbirth is martyrdom."
"23137","Sulayman ibn Dawud al-Hashimi narrated to us: Isma'il told us: Amr told us from al-Muttalib from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Guarantee for me six things from yourselves, I guarantee for you Paradise: be truthful when you speak, fulfill when you promise, render when you are entrusted, guard your private parts, lower your gazes, and restrain your hands."
"23138","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Muslim, narrated to us: Yazid, meaning Ibn Abi Ziyad, narrated to me from Isa ibn Fa'id from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no commander of ten but he is brought on the Day of Resurrection shackled; nothing frees him from it but his justice; and there is no man who learns the Qur'an then forgets it but he meets Allah on the Day of Resurrection maimed."
"23139","Abd al-Samad narrated to us: Thabit narrated to us from Asim from Salman, a man of the people of Sham, from Junadah from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, visiting him, with pain whose severity Allah, blessed and exalted, knows; then I entered upon him in the evening, and he had recovered excellently; so I said to him: I entered upon you in the morning with pain whose severity Allah knows, and I entered upon you in the evening recovered; then he said: O Ibn al-Samit, Jibril, peace be upon him, charmed me with an incantation and I recovered; shall I not teach it to you? I said: Yes; he said: In the name of Allah I charm you from everything that harms you, from the envy of every envier and the eye; in the name of Allah He heals you."
"23140","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban told us from Umayr ibn Hani that he heard Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah al-Kindi say: I heard Ubadah narrate from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that Jibril came to him while he was trembling with fever and said: In the name of Allah I charm you from everything that harms you, from the envy of an envier and every eye, and the name of Allah heals you."
"23141","Ali ibn Ayyash narrated to us: Ibn Thawban narrated to us, and he mentioned the like of it, except that he said: from the envy of an envier and from every eye; the name of Allah heals you."
"23142","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ayyash ibn Abi Rabi'ah from Sulayman ibn Musa from Abu Sallam from Abu Umamah from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: We went out with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and I witnessed Badr with him; then the people met, and Allah, blessed and exalted, routed the enemy; so a party went off in their tracks routing and killing, a party bent over the camp gathering and collecting it, and a party surrounded the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, lest the enemy catch him unaware; until when night came and the people returned to one another, those who gathered the spoils said: We collected and gathered it, so no one has a share in it; and those who went out seeking the enemy said: You are not more entitled to it than us; we drove the enemy from it and routed them; and those who surrounded the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: You are not more entitled to it than us; we surrounded the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, fearing the enemy would catch him unaware, and we were occupied with him; then revealed was: They ask you about the spoils; say: The spoils are for Allah and the Messenger; so fear Allah and set right relations among you; then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, divided it equally among the Muslims; he said: And the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he raided enemy land, would grant a fourth as extra, and when he returned with all the people, would grant a third; and he disliked the extra shares and would say: Let the strong of the believers return upon their weak."
"23143","Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Amr told us from Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil from Umar ibn Abd al-Rahman from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, told us about the Night of Decree, saying: It is in the month of Ramadan; so seek it in the last ten, for it is odd: the night of the twenty-first, or twenty-third, or twenty-fifth, or twenty-seventh, or the last night of Ramadan; whoever stands it seeking reward, forgiven for him what preceded of his sin."
"23144","Haywah ibn Shurayh and Yazid ibn Abd Rabbih both said: Baqiyyah narrated to us: Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to me from Khalid ibn Ma'dan from Amr ibn al-Aswad from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah that he narrated to them from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I have told you about the Dajjal until I feared you would not understand: the false messiah, the Dajjal, is a short man, bow-legged, curly-haired, one-eyed, his eye effaced, neither protruding nor sunken; then if he confuses you - Yazid said: about your Lord - then know that your Lord, blessed and exalted, is not one-eyed, and that you will not see your Lord, blessed and exalted, until you die; Yazid said: you see your Lord until you die."
"23145","Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated to us: Bahir ibn Sa'd narrated to me from Khalid ibn Ma'dan from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The Night of Decree is in the remaining ten; whoever stands them seeking their reward, then Allah, blessed and exalted, forgives him what preceded of his sin and what comes after; and it is an odd night: ninth, seventh, fifth, third, or the last night; and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The sign of the Night of Decree is that it is clear, bright, as if in it is a shining moon, calm, still, neither cold in it nor heat; and no star is permitted to be cast with in it until morning; and its sign is that the sun on its morning rises level, having no rays, like the moon on the night of full moon; and Satan is not permitted to come out with it that day."
"23146","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Bishr ibn Abdullah, meaning Ibn Yasar al-Sulami, narrated to us, saying: Ubadah ibn Nusayy narrated to me from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would be busy, and when an emigrant man came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he would entrust him to a man of us to teach him the Qur'an; so the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, entrusted a man to me, and he was with me in the house; I would give him the evening meal of the household, and I would teach him the Qur'an; then he departed to his family, and he saw he owed a debt, so he gifted me a bow the like of whose wood in quality and whose curve in beauty I never saw; then I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: What do you think, O Messenger of Allah, about it? He said: An ember between your shoulders you have shouldered - or you have hung upon yourself."
"23147","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Safwan narrated to us: Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Yazani narrated to me that a man asked Ubadah ibn al-Samit about the saying of Allah: For them is glad tidings in the life of this world; then Ubadah said: I asked the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: You have asked me about a matter no one of my community asked me about: it is the righteous vision which the believer sees or which is seen for him."
"23148","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us: Ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Aqil ibn Mudrik al-Sulami from Luqman ibn Amir from Abu Rashid al-Hubrani from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever worships Allah associating nothing with Him, establishes prayer, gives zakat, hears and obeys, then Allah, exalted, admits him through whichever of the gates of Paradise He wills, and they are eight gates; and whoever worships Allah associating nothing with Him, establishes prayer, gives zakat, hears and disobeys, then Allah, exalted, has the choice in his affair: if He wills He has mercy on him, and if He wills He punishes him."
"23149","Al-Hakam ibn Nafi' Abu al-Yaman narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym: Isma'il ibn Ubayd al-Ansari narrated to me, and he mentioned the hadith; then Ubadah said to Abu Hurayrah: O Abu Hurayrah, you were not with us when we pledged the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: we pledged him to hear and obey in energy and laziness, to spend in ease and hardship, to command right and forbid wrong, to speak concerning Allah, blessed and exalted, fearing no blame of any blamer therein, and to support the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he comes to us in Yathrib, protecting him as we protect ourselves, our wives, and our children, and for us is Paradise; so this is the pledge of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, which we pledged upon him; whoever breaks, breaks only upon himself; and whoever fulfills what he pledged the Messenger of Allah, Allah, blessed and exalted, fulfills what He pledged His Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon; then Mu'awiyah wrote to Uthman ibn Affan that Ubadah ibn al-Samit has corrupted Sham and its people against me: either gather Ubadah to you, or I leave him and Sham; so he wrote to him: Move Ubadah until you return him to his home in Madinah; so he sent Ubadah until he came to Madinah, and he entered upon Uthman in the house, with none in the house but a man of the forerunners or of the followers who had reached the people; and Uthman was surprised only by him sitting at the side of the house; so he turned to him and said: O Ubadah ibn al-Samit, what have we to do with you? Then Ubadah stood among the people and said - [source text breaks off here]."
"23150","I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, Abu al-Qasim Muhammad, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: After me men will govern your affairs who acquaint you with what you deny and deny you what you know; so no obedience to one who disobeys Allah, blessed and exalted; so do not make excuses by your Lord."
"23151","Al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Yazid ibn Sa'id from Abu Ata al-Saksaki from Mu'adh ibn Sa'd al-Saksaki from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah that he heard Ubadah ibn al-Samit mention that a man came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the span of ease of your community? He did not answer him until he asked him three times, each time not answering him; then the man left; then the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Where is the questioner? So they brought him back to him, and he said: You have asked me about a thing no one of my community asked me about: the span of ease of my community is one hundred years, he said it two or three times; then the man said: O Messenger of Allah, is there for that a sign, mark, or portent? He said: Yes: swallowing, quaking, and devils dispatched rallying against the people."
"23152","Al-Hakam ibn Nafi' narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Rashid ibn Dawud al-San'ani from Abd al-Rahman ibn Hassan from Rawh ibn Zinba' from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The companions missed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, one night, and when they halted they would lodge him in their middle; so they panicked and thought Allah, blessed and exalted, had chosen for him companions other than them; then there they were with the shape of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and they magnified Allah when they saw him; they said: O Messenger of Allah, we feared Allah, blessed and exalted, had chosen for you companions other than us; then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No; rather you are my companions in this world and the Hereafter; Allah, exalted, awakened me and said: O Muhammad, I sent no prophet nor messenger but he asked Me a request and I gave it to him; so ask, O Muhammad, you shall be given; so I said: My request is intercession for my community on the Day of Resurrection; then Abu Bakr said: O Messenger of Allah, what is intercession? He said: I say: O my Lord, my intercession which I stored with You; then the Lord, blessed and exalted, says: Yes; then my Lord, blessed and exalted, brings out the remainder of my community from the Fire and casts them into Paradise."
"23153","Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Qassab al-Basri narrated to us from Yunus ibn Ubayd from Muhammad ibn Sirin from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The house is sanctuary; so whoever enters your sanctuary against you, kill him."
"23155","Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us from Harb ibn Shaddad, saying: I heard Yahya ibn Abi Kathir say: It reached me that the chiefs are twelve, and he named Ubadah among them."
"23156","He said: I read to Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim from his father from Ibn Ishaq, saying: Ubadah ibn al-Samit ibn Qays ibn Asram ibn Fihr ibn Tha'labah is among the twelve who pledged the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, at the first Aqabah."
"23157","Yahya ibn Uthman Abu Zakariyya al-Nasri al-Harbi narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Abu Bakr ibn Abdullah from Abu Sallam from al-Miqdam ibn Ma'dikarib al-Kindi that he sat with Ubadah ibn al-Samit, Abu al-Darda, and al-Harith ibn Mu'awiyah al-Kindi, and they recalled the hadith of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; then Abu al-Darda said to Ubadah: O Ubadah, the words of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in such-and-such campaign concerning the fifths; then Ubadah said - Ishaq, meaning Ibn Isa, said in his hadith: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with them in their campaign toward a camel of the distributed spoils, and when he gave salam, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, stood, took a tuft of wool between his fingers and said: This is of your spoils, and I have in it but my share with you except the fifth, and the fifth is returned to you; so render the thread and the needle and greater than that and smaller; do not steal from spoils, for stealing from spoils is fire and shame upon its people in this world and the Hereafter; and strive against people in Allah, blessed and exalted, near and far, heed not in Allah the blame of any blamer, uphold the bounds of Allah in residence and travel, and strive in the way of Allah, for striving is a great gate of the gates of Paradise by which Allah, blessed and exalted, delivers from worry and grief."
"23158","Yahya ibn Uthman narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Sa'id ibn Yusuf from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir from Abu Sallam the like of that."
"23159","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us: al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us from Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit from Ubadah who said: Of the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is that the mine is void of liability, the well is void of liability, and the wound of a stray beast is void of liability; and the stray beast is the dumb animal of livestock and other than it; and void means wasted, not compensated; and he judged a fifth in buried treasure; and he judged that the fruit of palms belongs to one who pollinates them unless the buyer stipulates; and he judged that the wealth of the owned slave belongs to one who sold him unless the buyer stipulates; and he judged that the child is for the bed and for the adulterer is the stone; and he judged preemption among partners in lands and houses; and he judged for Hamal ibn Malik al-Hudhali his inheritance from his wife whom the other killed; and he judged in the slain fetus a fine of a male or female slave; he said: So her husband and her sons inherited her; he said: And he had children from both his wives; he said: Then the father of the killer, against whom judgment was passed, said: O Messenger of Allah, how do I pay for one who neither cried nor wailed, neither drank nor ate, so the like of that is void? Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This is of the soothsayers; he said: And he judged concerning the open space between the road, when its people want to build in it, that seven cubits be left for the road therein; he said: And that road was called al-Mita; and he judged concerning one, two, or three palms when they differ over rights thereof, that for each palm of those is reserved the reach of its fronds; and he judged concerning watering palms from the torrent that the upper drinks before the lower, and water is held to the ankles, then water is sent to the lower next to it, and thus orchards are finished or water runs out; and he judged that a woman gives nothing of her wealth except with her husband's permission; and he judged for the two grandmothers a sixth of inheritance between them equally; and he judged that whoever frees a share in a slave, upon him is completion of his freeing if he has wealth; and he judged there is no harm nor reciprocal harm; and he judged that a wrongfully seizing root has no right; and he judged among the people of Madinah concerning palms that the benefit of a well is not withheld; and he judged among the people of Madinah that surplus water is not withheld to withhold surplus pasture; and he judged in the major aggravated blood-money thirty she-camels in their third year, thirty in their fourth, and forty pregnant; and he judged in the minor blood-money thirty she-camels in their third year, thirty in their fourth, twenty she-camels in their second year, and twenty male camels in their second year; then camels rose in price after the death of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and dirhams fell, so Umar ibn al-Khattab valued the camels of Madinah at six thousand dirhams, an ounce per camel; then camels rose and silver fell, so Umar ibn al-Khattab added two thousand, two ounces per camel; then camels rose and dirhams fell, so Umar completed it at twelve thousand, three ounces per camel; he said: Then a third of blood-money was added in the sacred month and another third in the sacred land; he said: So the blood-money of the two sanctuaries was completed at twenty thousand; he said: And it was said: Taken from desert people from their livestock, they are not burdened with silver nor gold, and taken from each people the just value of their wealth."
"23160","Abdullah narrated to us: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud narrated to us: al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us from Ishaq ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit from Ubadah who said: Of the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, is: the mine is void of liability - and he mentioned the like of the long hadith of Abu Kamil, except that they differed in the chain: Abu Kamil said in his hadith from Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah that Ubadah said: Of the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; and al-Salt said from Ishaq ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah from Ubadah that: Of the judgment of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and he mentioned the hadith."
"23161","Abdullah narrated to us: Shayban ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us: al-Hasan narrated to us, saying: Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: Revealed upon the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was: And those who commit indecency - to the end of the verse; he said: So the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did that with them; then while the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was sitting with us around him - and when revelation descended upon him he turned away from us and we turned away from him, his face changed color, and he was distressed by it - then when revelation was lifted from him he said: Take from me; we said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah; he said: Allah has made for them a way: the virgin with the virgin: one hundred lashes and exile for a year; and the previously married with the previously married: one hundred lashes then stoning; al-Hasan said: I do not know whether it is of the hadith or not; he said: Then if they testify that the two were found in one cover without witnessing intercourse with which he mingled with her: one hundred lashes and their heads shaved."
"23162","Abdullah narrated to us: Ali ibn Shu'ayb al-Bazzar narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us: Abu Awanah told me from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad from Isa, saying: And he was governor over al-Raqqah, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no commander of ten but he is brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand chained to his neck until truth frees him or destroys him; and whoever learns the Qur'an then forgets it meets Allah maimed."
"23163","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Ahmad Makhlad ibn al-Hasan ibn Abi Zumayl narrated to us, dictating from his book: al-Hasan ibn Amr ibn Yahya al-Fazari narrated to us - kunya Abu Abdullah, laqab Abu al-Malih, meaning al-Raqqi - from Habib ibn Abi Marzuq from Ata ibn Abi Rabah from Abu Muslim who said: I entered the mosque of Hims, and in it was a circle of thirty-two men of the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; he said: And among them was a youth, dark-eyed, bright-toothed, sitting with legs drawn up; when they differed over anything they asked him, and he told them, and they stopped at his word; he said: I said: Who is this? They said: This is Mu'adh ibn Jabal; he said: Then I stood for prayer; he said: I wanted to meet one of them but could meet none of them; they left; then next day I entered, and there was Mu'adh praying toward a pillar; he said: So I prayed beside him, and when he finished I sat with the pillar between me and him, then sat with legs drawn up; I remained a while speaking not to him nor he to me; he said: Then I said: By Allah, I love you for other than worldly gain I hope to get from you nor kinship between me and you; he said: For what? He said: I said: For Allah, blessed and exalted; he said: Then he undid my sitting posture, then said: Then glad tidings if you are truthful, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Those who love one another in Allah, blessed and exalted, are in the shade of the Throne on a day no shade but His; envied for their place are the prophets and the martyrs; he said: Then I went out and met Ubadah ibn al-Samit; he said: So I told him of what Mu'adh had told me."
"23164","Then Ubadah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrate from his Lord, blessed and exalted, that He said: Deserved is My love upon those who visit one another for Me, and deserved is My love upon those who spend for one another for Me, upon pulpits of light envied for their place are the prophets and the truthful."
"23165","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Salih al-Hakam ibn Musa narrated to us: Hiql, meaning Ibn Ziyad, narrated to us from al-Awza'i: A man in the gathering of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me from Abu Idris al-Khawlani who said: I entered the mosque of Hims and sat with a circle of thirty-two men of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him; he said: A man of them would say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and narrate; then another would say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and narrate; he said: And among them was a man, dark-eyed, bright-toothed; when they doubted anything they referred it to him and were content with what he said therein; he said: I never sat before it nor after it a sitting like it; then the people dispersed, knowing the name of none of them nor his dwelling; he said: I spent a night the like of which I never spent; he said: And I said: I am a man seeking knowledge, and I sat with the companions of the Prophet of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, knowing the name of none of them nor his dwelling; then in the morning I went to the mosque, and there was the man to whom they referred when they doubted anything, bowing toward one of the pillars of the mosque; so I sat beside him, and when he finished I said: O servant of Allah, by Allah I love you for Allah, blessed and exalted; then he took my wrapped garment until he drew me to him, then said: You do love me for Allah? He said: I said: Yes, by Allah, I love you for Allah; he said: Then I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Those who love one another by the majesty of Allah are in the shade of Allah and the shade of His Throne on a day no shade but His; he said: Then I stood from him, and there was a man of the people who were with him; he said: I said: A hadith the man told me; he said: He tells you but truth."
"23166","He said: So I told him, and he said: I heard that and better than it: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, conveying from his Lord, blessed and exalted: Deserved is My love for those who love one another for Me, deserved is My love for those who spend for one another for Me, and deserved is My love for those who visit one another for Me; he said: I said: Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: I am Ubadah ibn al-Samit; he said: I said: Who is the man? He said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal."
"23167","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Bahr Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Abu Sinan from Ya'la ibn Shaddad who said: I heard Ubadah ibn al-Samit say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, visited me among a group of his companions and said: Do you know who the martyrs of my community are - two or three times - and they were silent; then Ubadah said: Tell us, O Messenger of Allah; then he said: The slain in the way of Allah is a martyr, the one dead of belly disease is a martyr, the one dead of plague is a martyr, and the woman in childbed is a martyr, her child dragging her by its cord to Paradise."
"23168","Abdullah narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Kawsaj told us: Muhammad ibn Yusuf told us: Ibn Thawban narrated to us from his father from Makhul from Jubayr ibn Nufayr that Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to them that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no Muslim man on the face of the earth who calls upon Allah, mighty and majestic, with a supplication but Allah gives it to him or wards off from him like it of evil, so long as he does not call with sin or severing of kinship."
"23169","Abdullah narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Sa'id al-Harawi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us from Ibn Khuthaym from Isma'il ibn Ubayd ibn Rifa'ah from his father Ubayd from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I heard Abu al-Qasim, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: After me men will govern your affairs who acquaint you with what you deny and make you deny what you know; so no obedience to one who disobeys Allah, exalted; so do not make excuses by your Lord."
"23170","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Harb narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us from Mansur from Hilal ibn Yasaf from Abu al-Muthanna from the nephew of Ubadah from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There will be rulers over you whom things distract from prayer until they delay it past its time; so pray it in its time; then a man said: O Messenger of Allah, if I catch it with them, do I pray? He said: If you wish."
"23171","Abdullah narrated to us: Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath and Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Naji both said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us from Jabalah ibn Atiyyah from Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn al-Samit from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever campaigns - Ibrahim said in his hadith: in the way of Allah, mighty and majestic - intending in his campaign nothing but a hobble-rope, he shall have what he intended."
"23172","Muhammad ibn Abbad, a Makkan, and Abu Marwan al-Uthmani Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Khalid both said: Abu Damrah narrated to us from Ibn Harmalah from Ya'la ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Hurmuz that Abdullah ibn Abbad al-Zuraqi told him that he used to hunt sparrows in the well of Abu Ihab, which belonged to them; then Ubadah saw me having taken a sparrow, took it from me and released it, and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made sacred what is between its two lava fields as Ibrahim made Makkah sacred; and Ubadah was of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"23173","Abdullah narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Kawsaj narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn told us: Sadaqah ibn Musa narrated to us from Farqad al-Sabakhi: Abu Munib al-Shami narrated to us from Abu Ata from Ubadah ibn al-Samit from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying - and Asim ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to me from Abu Umamah from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying - and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab narrated to me, or it was narrated to me from him, from Ibn Abbas from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: By Him in Whose hand is Muhammad's soul, people of my community shall spend the night in insolence, pride, play and diversion, and wake as apes and pigs for deeming forbidden things, singing girls, drinking wine, eating usury, and wearing silk lawful."
"23174","Abdullah narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Kawsaj narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn told us: Sadaqah ibn Musa narrated to us from Farqad al-Sabakhi: Abu Munib al-Shami narrated to us from Abu Ata from Ubadah ibn al-Samit from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying - and Asim ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to me from Abu Umamah from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying - and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab narrated to me, or it was narrated to me from him, from Ibn Abbas from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: By Him in Whose hand is Muhammad's soul, people of my community shall spend the night in insolence, pride, play and diversion, and wake as apes and pigs for deeming forbidden things, singing girls, drinking wine, eating usury, and wearing silk lawful."
"23175","Abdullah narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Kawsaj narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn told us: Sadaqah ibn Musa narrated to us from Farqad al-Sabakhi: Abu Munib al-Shami narrated to us from Abu Ata from Ubadah ibn al-Samit from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying - and Asim ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to me from Abu Umamah from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying - and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab narrated to me, or it was narrated to me from him, from Ibn Abbas from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: By Him in Whose hand is Muhammad's soul, people of my community shall spend the night in insolence, pride, play and diversion, and wake as apes and pigs for deeming forbidden things, singing girls, drinking wine, eating usury, and wearing silk lawful."
"23176","Abdullah narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Kawsaj narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Dukayn told us: Sadaqah ibn Musa narrated to us from Farqad al-Sabakhi: Abu Munib al-Shami narrated to us from Abu Ata from Ubadah ibn al-Samit from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him - and Shahr ibn Hawshab narrated to me from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying - and Asim ibn Amr al-Bajali narrated to me from Abu Umamah from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying - and Sa'id ibn al-Musayyab narrated to me, or it was narrated to me from him, from Ibn Abbas from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: By Him in Whose hand is Muhammad's soul, people of my community shall spend the night in insolence, pride, play and diversion, and wake as apes and pigs for deeming forbidden things, singing girls, drinking wine, eating usury, and wearing silk lawful."
"23177","Abdullah narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar narrated to us: One of the people of Sham whom I do not suspect narrated to me from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he saw the crescent would say: Allah is greatest; praise be to Allah; there is no power nor strength but with Allah; O Allah, I ask You the good of this month, and I seek refuge with You from the evil of decree and from the evil of gathering."
"23178","Abdullah narrated to us: Shuja' ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us from Mughirah from al-Sha'bi, saying: Ubadah ibn al-Samit said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever is wounded in his body with a wound then gives it as charity, Allah, mighty and majestic, expiates from him like what he gave as charity."
"23179","Ya'mar ibn Bishr narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Rishdin ibn Sa'd told us: Abu Hani al-Khawlani narrated to me from Amr ibn Malik al-Janbi that Fadalh ibn Ubayd and Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the Day of Resurrection comes and Allah, exalted, finishes judging creation, two men remain, and they are ordered to the Fire; then one of them turns, and the Almighty says: Bring him back; so they bring him back; He says to him: Why did you turn? He says: I hoped You would admit me to Paradise; he says: Then he is ordered to Paradise; then he says: Allah, mighty and majestic, has given me until if I fed the people of Paradise it would not diminish what is with me at all; he said: And when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned him, joy was seen in his face."
"23180","Abdullah narrated to us: Isma'il Abu Ma'mar al-Hudhali narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us from Mughirah from al-Sha'bi from Ibn al-Samit who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever gives charity from his body for anything, Allah, exalted, expiates from him to the measure of his sins."
"23181","Abdullah narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Salim al-Kufi al-Mafluj narrated to me - and he was trustworthy: Ubaydah ibn al-Aswad narrated to us from al-Qasim ibn al-Walid from Abu Sadiq from Rabi'ah ibn Najid from Ubadah ibn al-Samit that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, would take a tuft of wool from the side of the camel of the spoils and say: I have in it but like what one of you has of it; beware stealing from spoils, for stealing from spoils is disgrace upon its doer on the Day of Resurrection; render the thread and the needle and what is above that; and strive in the way of Allah, exalted, near and far, in residence and travel, for striving is a gate of the gates of Paradise; Allah, blessed and exalted, indeed delivers by it from worry and grief; and uphold the bounds of Allah among near and far, and let no blame of any blamer take you in Allah."
